  "notes": "Fasting (183-185): the crescent for the month, wheat for feeding a poor person, the book for the Quran, a door for ease, hands for the takbir. STAGING v4: Fasting: a family sitting at home at dusk (183-184); the moon for the fast, the counted days, wheat for the ransom of feeding (no purse: the ransom is food). One of them lowers his head on «مريضا». 185: believers reading in a prayer hall at night (the month the Quran was sent down), then saying the takbir (Al-Muyassar: takbir at the end of the fast). STAGING v4: Fasting: a family sitting at home at dusk (183-184); the moon for the fast, the counted days, wheat for the ransom of feeding (no purse: the ransom is food). One of them lowers his head on «مريضا». 185: believers reading in a prayer hall at night (the month the Quran was sent down), then saying the takbir (Al-Muyassar: takbir at the end of the fast)."
